SUMMARY:Conflict Navigation Skills Facilitated by Kyla Hartsfield
DESCRIPTION:✨Come learn how to make conflict your friend with three FREE in-person sessions. We will be digging into how to address conflict\, how to show up for conflict and how do we care for ourselves during and after conflict. You can sign up for one\, two or all three sessions! (You will get the most by attending all three sessions because they work with each other).\n✨This is a labor of love from me to my Durham community so please sign up and don’t hesitate to let me know if you have any questions! \n**Food will be provided** \n1. Address the Problem before the Party- learning different conflict styles and building steps to have the conversation before seeing the person at the club. Oct 20th 7-9pm\n2. The Capacity for Generative Conflict- conflict will always exist and it should. Conflict has brought great change to relationships\, communities and power imbalances. This session we will learn and practice skills for generative conflict. Oct 22nd 6:30-8:30pm\n3. How we care and return to ourselves during/after conflict- conflict can trigger us and general take an emotional toll. In this session we will discuss tools on how we can tend\, care and return to ourselves during and after conflict Oct 24th 1-3:30pm
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/conflict-navigation-skills-facilitated-by-kyla-hartsfield/2026-10-24/
LOCATION:Durham Burrow\, 207 N Church St\, Durham\, 27701
CATEGORIES:Classes & Workshops,Community Engagement,Diversity & Inclusivity,Free,Political/Activism
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/9DDBB880-65E5-42C3-9B23-FBBF1CB940D0-1.jpeg
GEO:35.995279;-78.8989921
